From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Sauve <paul@technove.co>
Date: Fri, 15 Jan 2021 19:05:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Pufferfish: Dynamic Activation of Brain

License: GPL-3.0-only (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html)
Original patch from Airplane/Pufferfish (https://github.com/pufferfish-gg/Pufferfish).
Ported to Reef 1.21.11 with reference to Leaf's version, including the
extra brain-based mobs added by Plazma.

Mobs that use the "brain" AI system (villagers, piglins, axolotls,
frogs, wardens, etc.) get their brain ticked less often the further
they are from the nearest player:

  ticks between brain ticks = (distance^2) >> activation-dist-mod,
  clamped between 1 and max-tick-freq.

Mobs within start-distance of a player are always ticked every tick.
Configured in reef.yml under optimizations.dynamic-activation-of-brain;
set enabled: false for vanilla behaviour. Villagers, axolotls, hoglins,
zombified piglins and goats are blacklisted by default.

